  "id": "COMPOUND:22101 - PROTEIN:5811",
  "verbalization": "Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide appears to interact with VMRC-LCP through multiple indirect pathways, with the most direct link emerging through its role as a target of SB-269970, which in turn targets VMRC-LCP. This suggests a potential regulatory relationship where Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide may influence VMRC-LCP via the enzyme Phosphatidylinositol 4-kinase type 2-beta. Complementary evidence points to another possible route, where Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide acts as a target of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1A4, which ultimately targets VMRC-LCP. These findings highlight a complex network of interactions, with the core mechanism likely involving the modulation of VMRC-LCP through downstream targets. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering multiple layers of regulation in understanding the biological role of Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide.",
